2026-10-01T17:48-07:00 ao-build-update scaffold created and deployed (README 5.2.1)

SCOPE
  Scaffolded the ao-build-update controlled software-update acquisition adapter.
  Deployed but deliberately NOT enabled. No workload was touched, no image was
  installed, no package upgraded, no service restarted.

CORRECTION TO README 5.1 GROUP B
  The group B row previously placed this adapter on "ao-admin (build/update
  duty)". ao-admin is Internal=true, which makes the adapter's only function
  impossible. Verified directly on this host:
    $ podman run --rm --network ao-admin alpine nslookup registry-1.docker.io
    ** server can't find registry-1.docker.io: NXDOMAIN
    $ podman run --rm --network ao-reporting-egress alpine nc -z registry-1.docker.io 443
    TCP OK
  A container on ao-admin cannot pull an image. The adapter was inert by
  construction. Placed instead on its own egress network ao-build-update,
  10.89.13.0/24, Internal=false, following the ao-reporting-egress precedent.
  Re-probed on the new network: DNS resolves, TCP 443 OK.

